  "notes": "{解雇|かいこ} means being dismissed from employment by the employer. It has a negative connotation as it is usually not voluntary.\n\nCommon types:\n- ⟦{懲戒|ちょうかい}→懲戒：09469_choukai⟧{解雇|かいこ} (disciplinary dismissal)\n- ⟦{整理|せいり}→整理：03297_seiri⟧{解雇|かいこ} (layoff, redundancy)\n- ⟦{不当|ふとう}→不当：11319_futou⟧{解雇|かいこ} (wrongful termination)\n\nRelated terms:\n- ⟦リストラ→リストラ：04689_risutora⟧ (restructuring, often euphemism for layoffs)\n- ⟦クビ→首：00792_kubi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧ (get fired - casual)\n- ⟦{首|くび}→首：00792_kubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{切|き}る→切る：02693_kiru⟧ (fire someone - casual)\n\nCultural note:\nJapanese labor law makes it difficult to fire employees without just cause. {解雇|かいこ} typically requires documented reasons and proper procedures.",
